    "answer": 0,
    "nudge": "Not quite. Spanish grew out of Latin. Which way round would the borrowing go?",
    "reveal": "Spanish inherited its verb endings from Latin almost unchanged, so your Spanish present tense gives you a head start. The Latin endings are -ō, -s, -t, -mus, -tis, -nt:",
